  recipeId: power
  concept: 'Authored objective: Calibrate and measure the emissions baseline.

    Authored
    requirement: Verify power, reference states and fixture response, then measure
    common and differential noise at idle.

    General teaching principle: Electrical
    measurements are differences or flows that require a correct reference, operating
    condition and fresh solver evidence.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence
    can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A pressure gauge needs a reference; a voltage measurement likewise depends
    on its defined points.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An expected rail or current is not a measured rail or current until
    the live circuit evidence confirms it.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Calibrate and measure the emissions baseline\u2019,
    which component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement
    should you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Calibrate and measure the emissions baseline\u2019, what
    result or observation would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish
    a predicted result from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 112, perform the objective \u2018Calibrate and measure the
    emissions baseline\u2019 in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence
    against: Verify power, reference states and fixture response, then measure common
    and differential noise at idle.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion; this
    tutorial does not grade your answer."
